up the equation and solve for \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ 66,200 = 20,000 \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[ 3.31 = \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\]\n\nThis equation can be solved iteratively using Python. Let's write the code to find the value of \\( r \\).\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import fsolve\n\n# Define the equation to solve\ndef equation(r):\n    return (1 + r)**3 - 1 - 3.31 * r\n\n# Initial guess for r\ninitial_guess = 0.05\n\n# Solve for r\nr_solution = fsolve(equation, initial_guess)[0]\n\n# Convert r to percentage\nr_percentage = r_solution * 100\nprint(r_percentage)\n```\n```output\n10.000000000000004\n```\nThe minimum compound interest rate that the savings account must provide is \\(\\boxed{10}\\)%.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the minimum compound interest rate that will allow the worker to have at least $66,200 in his savings account by the end of the third year, given that he deposits $20,000 at the end of each year.\n\nThe formula for the future value of a series of deposits (annuity) with compound interest is given by:\n\n\\[ FV = P \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^n - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( FV \\) is the future value of the deposits.\n- \\( P \\) is the amount of each deposit.\n- \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (in decimal form).\n- \\( n \\) is the number of years.\n\nIn this problem:\n- \\( FV = 66,200 \\)\n- \\( P = 20,000 \\)\n- \\( n = 3 \\)\n\nWe need to find the minimum \\( r \\) that satisfies the equation:\n\n\\[ 66,200 = 20,000 \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\nLet's solve this equation using Python. We'll use a numerical method to find the root of the equation.\n```python\nfrom scipy.optimize import fsolve\n\n# Define the function based on the equation\ndef equation(r):\n    return 20000 * ((1 + r)**3 - 1) / r - 66200\n\n# Initial guess for the interest rate\ninitial_guess = 0.05\n\n# Solve for the interest rate\ninterest_rate = fsolve(equation, 