art by noting that these side lengths form a right triangle with \\(C = 90^\\circ\\). Therefore, \\(\\sin C = \\sin 90^\\circ = 1\\).\n\nUsing the Law of Sines, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C} = 2R,\n\\]\nwhere \\(R\\) is the circumradius of the triangle. For a right triangle, the circumradius \\(R\\) is half the hypotenuse, so \\(R = \\frac{20}{2} = 10\\). Thus,\n\\[\n\\sin A = \\frac{a}{2R} = \\frac{12}{20} = \\frac{3}{5}, \\quad \\sin B = \\frac{b}{2R} = \\frac{16}{20} = \\frac{4}{5}.\n\\]\nSubstituting these values into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin C (a \\sin A + b \\sin B)}{\\sin A + \\sin B} = \\frac{1 \\left(12 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + 16 \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}\\right)}{\\frac{3}{5} + \\frac{4}{5}} = \\frac{12 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + 16 \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}}{\\frac{7}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{36}{5} + \\frac{64}{5}}{\\frac{7}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{100}{5}}{\\frac{7}{5}} = \\frac{100}{7} \\cdot \\frac{5}{5} = \\frac{100}{7} \\cdot 1 = 12.\n\\]\nThus, the value of the expression is \\(12\\).\n\nNext, we prove that for any triangle \\(ABC\\) with sides in the ratio \\(3:4:5\\), the value of the expression is always \\(12\\). Let the sides be \\(a = 3k\\), \\(b = 4k\\), and \\(c = 5k\\). Since these sides form a right triangle, \\(\\sin C = 1\\). Using the Law of Sines again, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C} = 2R.\n\\]\nFor a right triangle, the circumradius \\(R\\) is half the hypotenuse, so \\(R = \\frac{5k}{2}\\). Thus,\n\\[\n\\sin A = \\frac{a}{2R} = \\frac{3k}{5k} = \\frac{3}{5}, \\quad \\sin B = \\frac{b}{2R} = \\frac{4k}{5k} = \\frac{4}{5}.\n\\]\nSubstituting these values into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin C (a \\sin A + b \\sin B)}{\\sin A + \\sin B} = \\frac{1 \\left(3k \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + 4k \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}\\right)}{\\frac{3}{5} + \\frac{4}{5}} = \\frac{3k \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + 4k \\cdot \\frac{4}{5}}{\\frac{7}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{9k}{5} + \\frac{16k}