solve\n\n# Define the function representing the left-hand side of the equation\ndef equation(x):\n    term1 = (x + 1) * (x - 3) / (5 * (x + 2) * (x - 4))\n    term2 = (x + 3) * (x - 5) / (9 * (x + 4) * (x - 6))\n    term3 = -2 * (x + 5) * (x - 7) / (13 * (x + 6) * (x - 8))\n    return term1 + term2 + term3 - 92/585\n\n# Use fsolve to find the roots. We need to provide initial guesses for the roots.\ninitial_guesses = [-10, -5, 0, 5, 10]\nroots = []\nfor guess in initial_guesses:\n    root = fsolve(equation, guess)[0]\n    # Check if the root is real and hasn't been found before (with some tolerance)\n    if np.isreal(root) and not any(np.isclose(root, r, atol=1e-5) for r in roots):\n        roots.append(np.real(root))\n\n# Sort the roots\nroots = sorted(roots)\nprint(roots)\n```\n```output\n[-0.20000000000000018, 1.0000000000000002, 3.0, 4.000000000000001, 6.999999999999982]\n```\nThe real roots of the equation are approximately:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-0.2, 1, 3, 4, 7}\n\\]\n\nThese are the values of \\(x\\) that satisfy the given equation.", "To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to the right, we need to consider the following:\n\n1. A full spin is 360 degrees.\n2. After every full spin (360 degrees), the skater returns to the same direction she started in.\n3. Therefore, we need to find the equivalent angle within a single spin (0 to 360 degrees) by taking the remainder of 2250 divided by 360.\n\nThe remainder when 2250 is divided by 360 is the equivalent angle within one full spin. We can then determine the direction based on this equivalent angle.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Calculate the equivalent angle within one full spin\nequivalent_angle = 2250 % 360\nprint(equivalent_angle)\n```\n```output\n90\n```\nThe equivalent angle after spinning 2250 degrees is 90 degrees. Since the skater started facing north and spun 90 degrees to the right, she will now be facing east.\n\nTherefore, the direction the 