e the total degrees spun by 360:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2250}{360} = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater spins 6 full circles and an additional 0.25 of a circle.\n\n4. Determine the remaining degrees: Since 0.25 of a circle is 90 degrees (because \\(0.25 \\times 360 = 90\\)), the skater spins an additional 90 degrees.\n\n5. Add the remaining degrees to the starting position: The skater started at 0 degrees (north) and spins an additional 90 degrees. Thus, the final direction is:\n   \\[\n   0^\\circ + 90^\\circ = 90^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n6. Identify the final direction: 90 degrees corresponds to the direction east.\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the figure skater will be facing east. The final answer is:\n\n\\boxed{east}', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the problem**: The skater starts facing north and spins 2250 degrees to her right. We need to find her final direction.\n\n2. **Normalize the angle**: Since a full rotation is 360 degrees, we can reduce the angle by subtracting multiples of 360 degrees until we get an equivalent angle between 0 and 360 degrees.\n\n3. **Perform the calculation**:\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n4. **Calculate the remaining angle**:\n   \\[\n   2250 - (6 \\times 360) = 2250 - 2160 = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the final direction**: Starting from north and spinning 90 degrees to the right, the skater will face east.\n\nTherefore, the final direction the skater is facing is \\boxed{\\text{east}}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   - The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Convert the total degrees of rotation into full circles:**\n   - A full circle is 360 degrees.\n   - We need to find out how many full circles are in 2250 degrees.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2250 \\text{ degrees}}{360 \\text{ degrees/circle}} = 6.25 \\text{ circles}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the remaining degrees after completing full circles:**\n   - Since 6.25 circles include 6 full circles and a fraction of a circle, we calculate the remaining degrees.\n   \\[\n   2250 \\text{ degrees} - (6 \\times 360 \\text{ degrees}) = 2250 \\text{ degrees} - 2160 \\text{ degrees} = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Interpret the remaining degrees:**\n   - The skater has completed 6 full circles, which bring her back to her starting direction (north).\n   - She then spins an additional 90 degrees to the right.\n\n5. **Determine the final direction:**\n   - Starting from north and spinning 90 degrees to the right:\n     - North to East (90 degrees clockwise)\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the figure skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to the right, we need to understand that a full rotation is 360 degrees. Therefore, we can find the equivalent angle within one full rotation by calculating the remainder of 2250 divided by 360. This can be done using the modulo operation.\n\nLet\'s break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Calculate the equivalent angle within one full rotation.\n2. Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle.\n\nHere\'s the Python code to solve this:\n\n```python\n# Calculate the equivalent angle within one full rotation\nangle = 2250 % 360\n\n# Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle\nif angle == 0:\n    direction = "north"\nelif angle == 90:\n    direction = "east"\nelif angle == 180:\n    direction = "south"\nelif angle == 270:\n    direction = "west"\nelse:\n    # For angles between 0 and 90, 90 and 180, 180 and 270, and 270 and 360\n    if 0 < angle < 90:\n        direction = "east"\n    elif 90 < angle < 180:\n        direction = "south"\n    elif 180 < angle < 270:\n        direction = "west"\n    else:\n        direction = "north"\n\nprint(direction)\n```\n```output\neast\n```\nThe figure skater is facing \\(\\boxed{\\text{east}}\\) when she finishes her spin.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Convert the total degrees into full rotations:**\n   A full rotation is 360 degrees. We need to find out how many full rotations are in 2250 degrees.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of full rotations} = \\frac{2250}{360}\n   \\]\n   Performing the division:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2250}{360} = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and has an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Calculate the remaining degrees after full rotations:**\n   To find the remaining degrees:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Remaining degrees} = 2250 - (6 \\times 360)\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   2250 - 2160 = 90\n   \\]\n   So, after 6 full rotations, the skater has spun an additional 90 degrees.\n\n4. **Determine the direction after the remaining degrees:**\n   Starting from north, we need to move 90 degrees to the right:\n   - 0 degrees: North\n   - 90 degrees: East\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the skater is facing \\boxed{east}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the full rotation**: A full rotation is 360 degrees. This means that after every 360 degrees, the skater returns to her original direction.\n\n2. **Calculate the effective rotation**: Since 2250 degrees is more than one full rotation, we need to find out how many full rotations are contained in 2250 degrees and the remaining degrees after these full rotations. We do this by dividing 2250 by 360 and finding the remainder.\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 90\n   \\]\n   This means that 2250 degrees is equivalent to 6 full rotations plus an additional 90 degrees. Since the skater returns to her original direction after each full rotation, we only need to consider the remaining 90 degrees.\n\n3. **Determine the direction after 90 degrees**: If the skater starts facing north and spins 90 degrees to her right, she will face east. This is because:\n   - 0 degrees (or 360 degrees) is north\n   - 90 degrees is east\n   - 180 degrees is south\n   - 270 degrees is west\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}}.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the initial direction:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Convert the total degrees into full rotations:**\n   A full rotation is 360 degrees. We need to find out how many full rotations and additional degrees are in 2250 degrees.\n   \\[\n   2250 \\div 360 = 6.25\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full rotations and has an additional 0.25 of a rotation.\n\n3. **Calculate the additional degrees:**\n   To find the additional degrees, we multiply the decimal part by 360:\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\times 360 = 90\n   \\]\n   So, the skater spins an additional 90 degrees to her right.\n\n4. **Determine the final direction:**\n   Starting from north, spinning 90 degrees to the right means she will face east.\n\nTherefore, the skater is facing \\boxed{\\text{east}} when she finishes her spin.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees, we need to consider the fact that a full spin (360 degrees) brings her back to her original direction. Therefore, we can find the equivalent angle by taking the remainder of 2250 divided by 360. This will give us the angle relative to her starting direction.\n\nLet\'s calculate this step by step:\n\n1. Compute the equivalent angle by finding the remainder of 2250 divided by 360.\n2. Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle.\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these calculations:\n\n```python\n# Define the total degrees spun\ntotal_degrees = 2250\n\n# Calculate the equivalent angle by finding the remainder of 2250 divided by 360\nequivalent_angle = total_degrees % 360\n\n# Determine the direction based on the equivalent angle\nif equivalent_angle == 0:\n    direction = "north"\nelif 0 < equivalent_angle <= 90:\n    direction = "east"\nelif 90 < equivalent_angle <= 180:\n    direction = "south"\nelif 180 < equivalent_angle <= 270:\n    direction = "west"\nelif 270 < equivalent_angle < 360:\n    direction = "north"\n\nprint(direction)\n```\n```output\neast\n```\nThe figure skater is facing \\(\\boxed{\\text{east}}\\) after spinning 2250 degrees to her right.', 'To determine the direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Understand the starting position:**\n   The skater starts facing north.\n\n2. **Determine the total degrees in a full circle:**\n   A full circle is 360 degrees.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of full circles in 2250 degrees:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2250 \\text{ degrees}}{360 \\text{ degrees/circle}} = 6.25 \\text{ circles}\n   \\]\n   This means the skater completes 6 full circles and an additional 0.25 of a circle.\n\n4. **Convert the decimal part of the circle to degrees:**\n   \\[\n   0.25 \\text{ circles} \\times 360 \\text{ degrees/circle} = 90 \\text{ degrees}\n   \\]\n   So, the skater spins an additional 90 degrees after completing 6 full circles.\n\n5. **Determine the direction after spinning 90 degrees to the right from north:**\n   - Starting from north, spinning 90 degrees to the right means turning clockwise.\n   - North to east is 90 degrees clockwise.\n\nTherefore, after spinning 2250 degrees to her right, the skater is facing \\boxed{east}.', 'To solve this problem, we need to determine the final direction the figure skater is facing after spinning 2250 degrees to the right. We can break down the problem as follows:\n\n1. **Understand the Directions:**\n   - 0 degrees: North\n   - 90 degrees: East\n   - 180 degrees: South\n   - 270 degrees: West\n\n2. **Normalize the Angle:**\n   Since a full spin is 360 degrees, we can reduce the angle by finding the remainder when 2250 is divided by 360. This will give us the equivalent angle within one full spin.\n\n3. **Determine the Final Direction:**\n   Based on the normalized angle, we can determine the final direction.\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python using sympy to ensure accuracy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the total angle spun\ntotal_angle = 2250\n\n# Normalize the angle to be within 0 to 360 degrees\nnormalized_angle = total_angle % 360\n\n# Determine the final direction\nif normalized_angle == 0:\n    final_direction = "North"\nelif normalized_angle == 90:\n    final_direction = "East"\nelif normalized_angle == 180:\n    final_direction = "South"\nelif normalized_angle == 270:\n    final_direction = "West"\nelse:\n    # For other angles, we need to determine the closest direction\n    if 0 < normalized_angle < 90:\n        final_direction = "North"\n    elif 90 < normalized_angle < 180:\n        final_direction = "East"\n    elif 180 < normalized_angle < 270:\n        final_direction = "South"\n    elif 270 < normalized_angle < 360:\n        final_direction = "West"\n\nprint(final_direction)\n```\n```output\nWest\n```\nThe figure skater is facing \\(\\boxed{\\text{West}}\\) when she finishes her spin of 2250 degrees to the right.', "To solve this problem, we need to determine the direction of the skater after she has spun 2250 degrees. Since a full rotation is 360 degrees, we can find the equivalent angle by taking the remainder when 2250 is divided by 360. This will give us the angle rel