 seems that the output is quite complex and not simplified to a straightforward angle. Let's try to simplify the expression manually by recognizing patterns and using known trigonometric identities.\n\nGiven the expression:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ},\n\\]\nwe can use the identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B - \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A - B).\n\\]\n\nRewriting the numerator and denominator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 85^\\circ,\n\\]\nso the numerator becomes:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\cos (90^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$, we have $\\cos 85^\\circ = \\sin 5^\\circ$. So the numerator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nFor the denominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\sin (5^\\circ - 20^\\circ) = \\sin (-15^\\circ) = -\\sin 15^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = -\\sin (35^\\circ - 50^\\circ) = -\\sin (-15^\\circ) = \\sin 15^\\circ,\n\\]\nso the denominator becomes:\n\\[\n-\\sin 15^\\circ + \\sin 15^\\circ = 0.\n\\]\n\nThis suggests that the original expression might have been incorrectly simplified or there might be a different approach. Let's recheck the problem statement and consider another approach.\n\nGiven the complexity, let's directly compute the value of $\\tan \\theta$ using numerical methods to find the least positive angle $\\theta$.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\