or \\(\\tan \\theta\\) as:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can further simplify this expression by using the sum-to-product identities. The sum-to-product identities are:\n\n\\[\n\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A - \\sin B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right).\n\\]\n\nSo, we can rewrite the numerator and the denominator as:\n\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) becomes:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{-\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nThe least positive angle \\(\\theta\\) for which \\(\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}\\) is \\(120^\\circ\\). This is because \\(\\tan 120^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this by running the Python code.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Calculate the value of tan(theta)\r\nnumerator = math.cos(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) + math.cos(math.radians(35)) * math.cos(math.radians(50)) - math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.sin(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radians(35)) * math.sin(math.radians(50))\r\ndenominator = math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radian