os 50^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -(\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ) = -\\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = -\\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nSo the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can further simplify using the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ.\n\\]\nSo the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = -\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\n\nThus, $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$. The angle $\\theta$ for which $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$ is $150^\\circ$ (since $\\tan 150^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{150}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of tan(theta)\ntan_theta = (math.cos(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) + math.cos(math.radians(35)) * math.cos(math.radians(50)) - \n             math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.sin(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radians(35)) * math.sin(math.radians(50))) / \\\n            (math.sin(math.radians(5)) * math.cos(math.radians(20)) - math.sin(math.radians(35)) * math.cos(math.radians(50)) + \n             math.cos(math.radians(5)) * math.sin(math.radians(20)) - math.cos(math.radians(35)) * math.sin(math.radians(50)))\n\n# Calculate the angle theta in degrees\ntheta = math.degrees(math.atan(tan_theta))\n# Adjust the angle to be in the correct quadrant\nif tan_theta < 0:\n    theta += 180\n\nprint(theta)\n```", "To find the degree measure of the least positive angle $\\theta$ for which the given equation holds, we need to simplify the expression and then find the angle whose tangent is equal to the simplified expression.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use trigonometric identities to simplify the expression. Let's start by simplifying the numerator and the denominator separately.\n\nNumerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nDenominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the product-to-sum identities to simplify the terms. The product-to-sum identities are:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos (A+B) + \\cos (A-B)],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos (A-B) - \\cos (A+B)],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (A+B) + \\sin (A-B)],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin (A+B) - \\sin (A-B)].\n\\]\n\nLet's apply these identities to the given expression. We can simplify the numerator and denominator step by step.\n\nNumerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (5^\\circ - 20^\\circ)] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos (35^\