n to the equation \\(\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}\\) is \\(x = 11\\).\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the equation $\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}$, we'll start by eliminating the fractions. This can be done by cross-multiplying. Cross-multiplication involves multiplying the numerator of the left fraction by the denominator of the right fraction and setting it equal to the numerator of the right fraction times the denominator of the left fraction. This gives us:\n\\[ 2(x-5) = 3 \\cdot 4.\\]\n\nSimplifying the right side of the equation, we get:\n\\[ 2(x-5) = 12.\\]\n\nNext, we'll distribute the $2$ on the left side of the equation:\n\\[ 2x - 10 = 12.\\]\n\nTo isolate $x$, we'll add $10$ to both sides of the equation:\n\\[ 2x = 22.\\]\n\nFinally, we'll divide both sides of the equation by $2$ to solve for $x$:\n\\[ x = 11.\\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation $\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}$ is $x = 11$.", "To solve the equation \\(\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}\\), we can use the method of cross-multiplication. Cross-multiplying gives us:\n\n\\[2(x-5) = 3 \\cdot 4.\\]\n\nSimplifying the right side, we get:\n\n\\[2(x-5) = 12.\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 2:\n\n\\[x-5 = 6.\\]\n\nFinally, we add 5 to both sides to isolate \\(x\\):\n\n\\[x = 11.\\]\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the equation components\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols('x')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = Eq(2/3, 4/(x-5))\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[11.0000000000000]\n```\nThe solution to the equation \\(\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}\\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the equation $\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}$, we can use the method of cross-multiplication. This method involves multiplying the numerator of the left fraction by the denominator of the right fraction and setting it 