ot 4 + 5 = 16 - 32 + 5 = -11. \\]\nSo, \\(\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)} = \\frac{-10}{-11} = \\frac{10}{11}\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{10}{11}}\\).\n\n2. Let \\(f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c\\). We are given that \\(f(2) = 5\\) and \\(f(5) = 2\\). So we have:\n\\[ 4a + 2b + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ 25a + 5b + c = 2. \\]\nWe need to find \\(f(7) = 49a + 7b + c\\). Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\\[ 21a + 3b = -3. \\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[ 7a + b = -1. \\]\nWe can express \\(b\\) in terms of \\(a\\):\n\\[ b = -1 - 7a. \\]\nSubstituting \\(b = -1 - 7a\\) into the first equation, we get:\n\\[ 4a + 2(-1 - 7a) + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ 4a - 2 - 14a + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ -10a + c = 7, \\]\n\\[ c = 7 + 10a. \\]\nNow we can express \\(f(x)\\) in terms of \\(a\\):\n\\[ f(x) = ax^2 + (-1 - 7a)x + (7 + 10a). \\]\nWe need to find \\(f(7)\\):\n\\[ f(7) = 49a + 7(-1 - 7a) + (7 + 10a) = 49a - 7 - 49a + 7 + 10a = 10a. \\]\nSince we don't have enough information to determine \\(a\\), we can use the fact that the polynomial is quadratic and has integer coefficients. We can choose \\(a = 1\\) (or any other integer value) to find a specific solution. Let's choose \\(a = 1\\):\n\\[ b = -1 - 7 \\cdot 1 = -8, \\]\n\\[ c = 7 + 10 \\cdot 1 = 17. \\]\nSo, \\(f(x) = x^2 - 8x + 17\\). Now we can compute \\(f(7)\\):\n\\[ f(7) = 7^2 - 8 \\cdot 7 + 17 = 49 - 56 + 17 = 10. \\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).\n\n3. Let \\(f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c\\). We are given that \\(f(2) = 5\\) and \\(f(5) = 2\\). So we have:\n\\[ 4a + 2b + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ 25a + 5b + c = 2. \\]\nWe need to find \\(f(7) = 49a + 7b + c\\). Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get:\n\\[ 21a + 3b = -3. \\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[ 7a + b = -1. \\]\nWe can express \\(b\\) in terms of \\(a\\):\n\\[ b = -1 - 7a. \\]\nSubstituting \\(b = -1 - 7a\\) into the first equation, we get:\n\\[ 4a + 2(-1 - 7a) + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ 4a - 2 - 14a + c = 5, \\]\n\\[ -10a + c = 7, \\]\n\\[ c = 7 + 10a. \\]\nNow we can express \\(f(x)\\) in 