_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211\\]\n\\[x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420\\]\n\\[x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is:\n\\[211 + 420 + 267 = 898\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence until we see the pattern repeats\nfor n in range(4, 20):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# The sequence repeats every 10 terms, so we can use modulo 10 to find the values\nx_531 = x[531 % 10 - 1]\nx_753 = x[753 % 10 - 1]\nx_975 = x[975 % 10 - 1]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to understand the recurrence relation given: $x_{n} = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4}$. We will use the initial values $x_1 = 211$, $x_2 = 375$, $x_3 = 420$, and $x_4 = 523$ to generate subsequent terms and observe if there is any periodicity.\n\nFirst, let's generate a few more terms to see if we can identify a pattern:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_5 &= x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_6 &= x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_7 &= x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_8 &= x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_9 &= x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{10} &= x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{11} &= x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{12} &= x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that $x_{11} = x_1$ and $x_{12} = x_2$, which suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, we can use this periodicity to find the values of $x_{531}$, $x_{753}$, and $x_{975}$:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_{531} &= x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\\\\nx_{753} &= x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\\\\nx_{975} &= x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the value of $x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}$:\n\n\\[\nx_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898.\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{898}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [0] * 1000\nx[1], x[2], x[3], x[4] = 211, 375, 420, 523\n\n# Generate the sequence using the recurrence relation\nfor n in range(5, 1000):\n    x[n] = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n\n# Calculate the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[531 % 10]\nx_753 = x[753 % 10]\nx_975 = x[975 % 10]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```", "To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\( p \\) that satisfy both inequalities:\n\n1. \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\)\n2. \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\)\n\nLet's solve each inequality separately and then find the intersection of the solutions.\n\n### Solving the first inequality: \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\)\n\n\\[\n0 \\ge 54p - 144\n\\]\n\\[\n144 \\ge 54p\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{144}{54} \\ge p\n\\]\n\\[\np \\le \\frac{144}{54} = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\n\nSo, the solution to the first inequality is \\( p \\le \\frac{8}{3} \\).\n\n### Solving the second inequality: \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\)\n\n\\[\n0 > 12 - 20p\n\\]\n\\[\n20p > 12\n\\]\n\\[\np > \\frac{12}{20} = \\frac{3}{5}\n\\]\n\nSo, the solution to the second inequality is \\( p > \\frac{3}{5} \\).\n\n### Finding the intersection of the solutions\n\nThe values of \\( p \\) that satisfy both inequalities must be in the interval \\( \\left( \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{8}{3} \\right] \\).\n\nThe final answer in interval notation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{8}{3} \\right]}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, solve, S\r\n\