ion $\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}=\\frac{3}{2}$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Square both sides of the equation to eliminate the square roots.\n2. Simplify the resulting equation to solve for $x$.\n3. Verify the solution to ensure it satisfies the original equation.\n\nLet's start by squaring both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2x}{3x-1} = \\frac{9}{4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we can cross-multiply to solve for $x$:\n\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 2x = 9 \\cdot (3x - 1)\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n8x = 27x - 9\n\\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[\n8x - 27x = -9\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-19x = -9\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by -19, we get:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{9}{19}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's verify this solution by substituting $x = \\frac{9}{19}$ back into the original equation to ensure it satisfies $\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}=\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2 \\cdot \\frac{9}{19}}}{\\sqrt{3 \\cdot \\frac{9}{19} - 1}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{18}{19}}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{19} - \\frac{19}{19}}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\frac{18}{19}}}{\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{19}}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{18}}{\\sqrt{8}} = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSince the left side simplifies to $\\frac{3}{2}$, the solution $x = \\frac{9}{19}$ is correct. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{9}{19}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve, sqrt\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation\r\nequation = Eq(sqrt(2*x) / sqrt(3*x - 1), 3/2)\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\r\nprint(solution)\n```", "Let's solve the equation step-by-step.\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we can square both sides to eliminate the square roots:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{