 of \\(8^6\\) is the same as the units digit of \\(8^2\\), which is 4.\n\nTherefore, the units digit of \\(18^6\\) is 4.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to find the units digit of a number raised to a power\r\ndef units_digit(base, exponent):\r\n    # We only need the units digit of the base\r\n    base_units_digit = base % 10\r\n    # Find the units digit of the base raised to the exponent\r\n    units_digit_result = pow(base_units_digit, exponent, 10)\r\n    return units_digit_result\r\n\r\n# Find the units digit of 18^6\r\nunits_digit_18_6 = units_digit(18, 6)\r\nprint(units_digit_18_6)\n```\n```output\n4\n```\nThe units digit of \\(18^6\\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", 'Find the units digit of $22^{8}.$ 22\nFind the units digit of $23^{11}.$ 3\nFind the units digit of $24^{13}.$ 4\nFind the units digit of $25^{14}.$ 5\nFind the units digit of $26^{15}.$ 6\nFind the units digit of $27^{16}.$ 7\nFind the units digit of $28^{17}.$ 8\nFind the units digit of $29^{18}.$ 9\nFind the units digit of $30^{19}.$ 0\nFind the units digit of $31^{20}.$ 1\nFind the units digit of $32^{21}.$ 2\nFind the units digit of $33^{22}.$ 3\nFind the units digit of $34^{23}.$ 4\nFind the units digit of $35^{24}.$ 5\nFind the units digit of $36^{25}.$ 6\nFind the units digit of $37^{26}.$ 7\nFind the units digit of $38^{27}.$ 8\nFind the units digit of $39^{28}.$ 9\nFind the units digit of $40^{29}.$ 0\nFind the units digit of $41^{30}.$ 1\nFind the units digit of $42^{31}.$ 2\nFind the units digit of $43^{32}.$ 3\nFind the units digit of $44^{33}.$ 4\nFind the units digit of $45^{34}.$ 5\nFind the units digit of $46^{35}.$ 6\nFind the units digit of $47^{36}.$ 7\nFind the units digit of $48^{37}.$ 8\nFind the units digit of $49^{38}.$ 9\nFind the units digit of $50^{39}.$ 0\nFind the units digit of $51^{40}.$ 1\nFind the units digit of $52^{41}.$ 2\nFind the units digit of $53^{42}.$ 3\nFind the units digit of $54^{43}.$ 4\nFind the units digit of $55^{44}.$ 5\nF