 = 3BD^2 - \\frac{BD^2}{1000}\n     \\]\n   - Simplifying further:\n     \\[\n     970 = BD^2 \\left(3 - \\frac{1}{1000}\\right) = BD^2 \\left(\\frac{2999}{1000}\\right)\n     \\]\n   - Solving for \\(BD^2\\):\n     \\[\n     BD^2 = \\frac{970 \\cdot 1000}{2999} = \\frac{970000}{2999}\n     \\]\n   - Taking the square root:\n     \\[\n     BD = \\sqrt{\\frac{970000}{2999}} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\n     \\]\n\n7. **Find \\(x\\):**\n   - In triangle \\(BDA\\), \\(\\tan(\\theta) = \\frac{BD}{10} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{970}}{10\\sqrt{2999}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\).\n   - Since \\(\\tan(\\theta) = \\frac{BD}{10}\\), we have:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{BD}{10} = \\frac{\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\n     \\]\n   - So, \\(BD = \\frac{10\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\).\n   - Using the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\(BDA\\):\n     \\[\n     AB^2 = AD^2 + BD^2 = 10^2 + \\left(\\frac{10\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\right)^2 = 100 + \\frac{970000}{2999} = 100 + 323.44 = 423.44\n     \\]\n   - So, \\(AB = \\sqrt{423.44} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1270000}{2999}} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{1270}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\).\n\n8. **Find the Perimeter:**\n   - The perimeter of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\(AB + AC + BC = 2AB + 2x\\).\n   - Since \\(AB = \\frac{10\\sqrt{1270}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\), and \\(x = \\sqrt{121 + x^2}\\), we need to find \\(x\\).\n   - Using the fact that \\(BD = \\frac{10\\sqrt{970}}{\\sqrt{2999}}\\) and \\(DM = 1\\), we can find \\(x\\).\n   - The perimeter is \\(2 \\cdot \\frac{10\\sqrt{1270}}{\\sqrt{2999}} + 2x\\).\n\nLet's calculate the exact value using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nAM = 11\nAD = 10\nDM = AM - AD\n\n# Calculate BD using the derived formula\nBD = math.sqrt(970000 / 2999)\n\n# Calculate AB using Pythagorean theorem in triangle BDA\nAB = math.sqrt(AD**2 + BD**2)\n\n# Calculate x using the fact that AB = sqrt(121 + x^2)\nx = math.sqrt(AB**2 - 121)\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of triangle ABC\nperimeter = 2 * AB + 2 * x\n