 are 5 cm and 9 cm.\n- The height of the trapezoid is 5 cm.\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the lengths of the bases and the height\nb1 = 5  # length of the first base in cm\nb2 = 9  # length of the second base in cm\nh = 5   # height of the trapezoid in cm\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (b1 + b2) * h\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\( \\boxed{35} \\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (b_1 + b_2) \\times h \\]\n\nwhere \\( b_1 \\) and \\( b_2 \\) are the lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) and \\( h \\) is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that:\n- The lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) are 5 cm and 9 cm.\n- The height of the trapezoid is 5 cm.\n\nNow we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 14 \\times 5 = 35 \\text{ square centimeters} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the lengths of the bases and the height of the trapezoid\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 9\nheight = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that:\n- The height of the trapezoid is 9 cm.\n- The lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) are 5 cm and 5 + 3 = 8 cm.\n\nSo, substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 8) \\times 9 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\times 9 = \\frac{117}{2} = 58.5 \\text{ square centimeters} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the bases and height of the trapezoid\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 5 + 3\nheight = 9\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n58.5\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{58.5}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that:\n- The lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) are 5 cm and 9 cm.\n- The height of the trapezoid is 5 cm.\n\nPlugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the bases and height of the trapezoid\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 9\nheight = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the trapezoid, we can use the formula for the area of a trapezoid:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (b_1 + b_2) \\times h \\]\n\nwhere \\( b_1 \\) and \\( b_2 \\) are the lengths of the two parallel sides (bases) and \\( h \\) is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see:\n- The length of the top base \\( b_1 \\) is 5 cm.\n- The length of the bottom base \\( b_2 \\) is 9 cm.\n- The height \\( h \\) is 5 cm.\n\nNow we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (5 + 9) \\times 5 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the bases and height of the trapezoid\nb1