n Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nusd_to_pounds = 1.64\nusd_to_euros = 1.32\ninitial_usd = 300\n\n# Amount to be withdrawn in USD\nwithdrawn_usd = initial_usd / 2\n\n# Convert withdrawn USD to pounds and euros\nwithdrawn_pounds = withdrawn_usd / usd_to_pounds\nwithdrawn_euros = withdrawn_usd / usd_to_euros\n\n# Calculate the difference between euros and pounds\ndifference = withdrawn_euros - withdrawn_pounds\n\n# Round to the nearest whole number\ndifference_rounded = round(difference)\n\nprint(difference_rounded)\n```\n```output\n22\n```\nThe difference between the number of euros and pounds that Kathy will have is \\(\\boxed{22}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate how much money Kathy is withdrawing in US dollars.\n2. Convert the US dollars to British pounds and euros.\n3. Calculate the difference between the amount of euros and pounds.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy.\n\n1. Kathy has 300 US dollars and wants to withdraw half of it in British pounds and half in euros. So she will withdraw 150 US dollars in British pounds and 150 US dollars in euros.\n2. Convert 150 US dollars to British pounds using the exchange rate 1 pound = 1.64 USD.\n3. Convert 150 US dollars to euros using the exchange rate 1 euro = 1.32 USD.\n4. Calculate the difference between the amount of euros and pounds.\n\nLet's implement this in Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nusd_amount = 300\npounds_rate = 1.64\neuros_rate = 1.32\n\n# Amount to withdraw in US dollars\nwithdraw_amount_usd = usd_amount / 2\n\n# Convert US dollars to British pounds\nwithdraw_amount_pounds = withdraw_amount_usd / pounds_rate\n\n# Convert US dollars to euros\nwithdraw_amount_euros = withdraw_amount_usd / euros_rate\n\n# Calculate the difference between euros and pounds\ndifference = withdraw_amount_euros - withdraw_amount_pounds\n\n# Round to the nearest whole number\ndifference_rounded = round(difference)\n\nprint(difference_rounded)\