at).\n   - The parallelogram has an area equal to \\( \\frac{1}{8} \\) of the square (since it is the same size as a medium triangle).\n\n4. **Determine the area of the gray piece:**\n   - The gray piece is one of the large isosceles triangles, so its area is \\( \\frac{1}{4} \\) of the square.\n\nLet\'s calculate this using Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the area of the square\narea_square = 16\n\n# Calculate the area of the gray piece (one of the large isosceles triangles)\narea_gray_piece = area_square / 4\n\nprint(area_gray_piece)\n```\n```output\n4.0\n```\nThe area of the gray piece, which is one of the large isosceles triangles, is \\(\\boxed{4}\\) square inches.', 'To solve this problem, let\'s start by determining the side length of the square $ABCD$. Since the area of the square is 16 square inches, the side length of the square is $\\sqrt{16} = 4$ inches.\n\nNext, let\'s analyze the tangram pieces. The tangram consists of seven pieces: five isosceles triangles, one square, and one parallelogram. The area of the square piece "e" is the same as the area of the smallest triangle. Let\'s denote the side length of the square "e" as $s$. Since the area of the square "e" is the same as the area of the smallest triangle, and the smallest triangle is half the area of the square "e" (because it is an isosceles right triangle with legs equal to $s$), we can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area of square "e"} = s^2 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area of smallest triangle} = \\frac{1}{2} s^2 \\]\n\nSince the area of the smallest triangle is also the area of the square "e", we have:\n\n\\[ s^2 = \\frac{1}{2} s^2 \\]\n\nThis equation is not correct as written, but it implies that the area of the smallest triangle is half the area of the square "e". Since the total area of the square $ABCD$ is 16 square inches, and the tangram pieces together make up the entire square, we can deduce that the area of the gray piece can be found by subtracting 