\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon (hybrid car)}} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{48 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 250 \\text{ gallons}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the difference in gasoline consumption between the SUV and the hybrid car:\n\\[\n\\text{Gasoline saved} = \\text{Gasoline consumption for SUV} - \\text{Gasoline consumption for hybrid car} = 800 \\text{ gallons} - 250 \\text{ gallons} = 550 \\text{ gallons}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Karla would have saved \\boxed{550} gallons of gasoline last year by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of an SUV.", 'To determine how many gallons of gasoline Karla would have saved by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the SUV:**\n   - The SUV averages 15 miles per gallon.\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - Total gallons used by the SUV:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by SUV} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon (SUV)}} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{15 \\text{ miles/gallon}} = 800 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the hybrid car:**\n   - The hybrid car averages 48 miles per gallon.\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - Total gallons used by the hybrid car:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon (hybrid car)}} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{48 \\text{ miles/gallon}} = 250 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the gallons of gasoline saved:**\n   - Subtract the gallons used by the hybrid car from the gallons used by the SUV:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons saved} = \\text{Gallons used by SUV} - \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = 800 \\text{ gallons} - 250 \\text{ gallons} = 550 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, Karla would have saved \\boxed{550} gallons of gasoline last year by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV.', 'To d