e equation:\n\n\\[ \\frac{255}{512} = \\frac{1}{4} \\frac{1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{255}{512} = \\frac{1}{4} \\frac{1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n}{\\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 \\left(1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n\\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\left(1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n\\right) \\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{255}{256} = 1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n \\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n = 1 - \\frac{255}{256} = \\frac{1}{256} \\]\n\nSince $\\frac{1}{256} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^8$, we can conclude that:\n\n\\[ n = 8 \\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\na = 1/4  # first term\nr = 1/2  # common ratio\nS_n = 255/512  # sum of the first n terms\n\n# Function to calculate the sum of the first n terms of a geometric sequence\ndef geometric_sum(a, r, n):\n    return a * (1 - r**n) / (1 - r)\n\n# Iterate to find the value of n\nn = 1\nwhile geometric_sum(a, r, n) != S_n:\n    n += 1\n\nprint(n)\n```\n```output\n8\n```\nThe value of $n$ for which the sum of the first $n$ terms of the geometric sequence $\\left\\{\\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{8}, \\frac{1}{16}, \\dots \\right\\}$ is $\\frac{255}{512}$ is $\\boxed{8}$.", "To find the value of \\( n \\) for which the sum of the first \\( n \\) terms of the geometric sequence \\(\\left\\{\\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{8}, \\frac{1}{16}, \\dots \\right\\}\\) is \\(\\frac{255}{512}\\), we can use the formula for the sum of the first \\( n \\) terms of a geometric series:\n\n\\[ S_n = a \\frac{1 - r^n}{1 - r} \\]\n\nwhere \\( a \\) is the first term, \\( r \\) is the common ratio, and \\( n \\) is the number of terms. For the given sequence:\n\n- The first term \\( a = \\frac{1}{4} \\).\n- The common ratio \\( r = \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{1}{4} \\frac{1 - \\left(\\