 given scale of the map. The scale tells us that 3 inches on the map correspond to 10 miles in real life. We can set up a proportion to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles.\n\nThe proportion can be set up as follows:\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the distance on the map\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles / 10) * real_life_distance\n\n# Convert the result to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint((map_distance, map_distance_fraction))\n```\n```output\n(15.975000000000001, Fraction(639, 40))\n```\nThe distance on the map corresponding to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the distance on the map that corresponds to a real-life distance of 53.25 miles, given that 3 inches on the map represents 10 miles in real life.\n\nFirst, we can find out how many miles one inch on the map represents:\n\\[ \\text{Miles per inch} = \\frac{10 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ inches}} \\]\n\nThen, to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life, we can use the following formula:\n\\[ \\text{Distance on map} = \\frac{53.25 \\text{ miles}}{\\text{Miles per inch}} = \\frac{53.25 \\text{ miles}}{\\frac{10 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ inches}}} = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_distance_miles = 53.25  # real distance in miles\nmap_distance_inches 