s \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\(15.975\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{15975}{1000}\\). Simplifying this fraction, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use it to convert the real-life distance between the two buildings to the corresponding distance on the map.\n\nGiven:\n- 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life.\n- The real-life distance between the two buildings is 53.25 miles.\n\nWe can set up a proportion to find the distance on the map. Let's denote the distance on the map by \\(d\\) inches. The proportion can be written as:\n\\[ \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{d \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nFrom this proportion, we can solve for \\(d\\):\n\\[ d = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the distance on the map\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_life_distance) / 10\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance on the map between the two buildings is \\(15.975\\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\(15.975\\) is the same as \\(15 \\frac{39}{40}\\) or \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\).\n\nThus, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use it to find the distance between the two buildings on the map.\n\nGiven:\n- 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life.\n- The real-life distance between the two buildings is 53.25 miles.\n\nFirst, we need to find out how many miles correspond to 1 inch on the map. Since 3 inches on the map correspond to 10 miles in real life, 1 inch on the map corresponds to $\\frac{10}{3}$ miles in real life.\n\nNext, we need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life. If 1 inch on the map corresponds to $\\frac{10}{3}$ miles in real life, then the distance $d$ in inches on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life is given by:\n\\[ d = \\frac{53.25 \\text{ miles}}{\\frac{10}{3} \\text{ miles/inch}} = 53.25 \\times \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_distance = 53.25  # in miles\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # in inches\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = real_distance * (map_distance_per_10_miles / 10)\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is 15.975 inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that 15.975 is the same as $\\frac{15975}{1000}$. We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nThe GCD of 15975 and 1000 is 25. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 25, we get:\n\\[ \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "Let's solve the problem step-by-step.\n\n1. First, we need to determine the scale of the map. The scale is given as 3 inches on the map equates to 10 miles in real life. So, the scale can be expressed as a ratio: $\\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}}$.\n\n2. To find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life, we can set up a proportion:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}}\n   \\]\n   Solving for $x$:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}}\n   \\]\n\n3. Let's calculate the value of $x$ using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nscale_map_inches = 3\nscale_real_miles = 10\nreal_distance_miles = 53.25\n\n# Calculate the distance on the map\nmap_distance_inches = (scale_map_inches * real_distance_miles) / scale_real_miles\nprint(map_distance_inches)\n```\n```output\n15.975\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is $15.975$ inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that $15.975$ can be written as $\\frac{15975}{1000}$. Simplifying this fraction, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15975 \\div 125}{1000 \\div 125} = \\frac{127.8}{8} = \\frac{1278}{80} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}$ inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use it to convert the real-life distance to the map distance.\n\nGiven:\n- 3 inches on the map represents 10 miles in real life.\n\nWe need to find out how many inches on the map represent 53.25 miles in real life.\n\nFirst, we calculate the scale of the map. The scale is the ratio of the map distance to the real distance. From the given information, the scale is:\n\\[ \\text{Scale} = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nNow, we can use this scale to find the map distance corresponding to 53.25 miles in real life. Let \\( x \\) be the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life. Then:\n\\[ x = 53.25 \\text{ miles} \\times \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression to find \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\nscale_numerator = 3  # inches\nscale_denominator = 10  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance\nmap_distance = (real_distance * scale_numerator) / scale_denominator\nprint(map_distance)\n```\n```output\n15.975000000000001\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\( 15.975 \\) inches. To express this as a fraction, we recognize that \\( 15.975 \\) is the same as \\( \\frac{15975}{1000} \\). We can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 15975 and 1000.\n\nThe GCD of 15975 and 1000 is 25. Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by 25, we get:\n\\[ \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo the distance between the buildings on the map is \\( \\frac{639}{40} \\) inches.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use that scale to find the distance on the map corresponding to the real-life distance of 53.25 miles.\n\n1. First, we need to determine the scale of the map. The scale is given as 3 inches on the map equating to 10 miles in real life. This means that 1 inch on the map corresponds to $\\frac{10}{3}$ miles in real life.\n\n2. Next, we need to find the distance on the map that corresponds to 53.25 miles in real life. We can use the scale to set up the following proportion:\n\\[ \\text{Distance on map (in inches)} = \\frac{53.25 \\text{ miles}}{\\frac{10}{3} \\text{ miles/inch}} = 53.25 \\times \\frac{3}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\n3. Simplifying the expression, we get:\n\\[ \\text{Distance on map (in inches)} = \\frac{53.25 \\times 3}{10} = \\frac{159.75}{10} = \\frac{159.75 \\times 100}{10 \\times 100} = \\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nreal_life_distance = 53.25  # miles\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\n\n# Calculate the scale (inches per mile)\nscale = map_distance_per_10_miles / 10  # inches per mile\n\n# Calculate the distance on the map\ndistance_on_map = real_life_distance * scale  # inch