ment this step-by-step in Python:\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the matrix M\na, b, c, d = 4, -1, 2, 1\nM = sp.Matrix([[a, b], [c, d]])\n\n# Define the line y = 2x + 1\nx = sp.symbols('x')\ny = 2*x + 1\n\n# Find the image of the line under M\npoint = sp.Matrix([x, y])\nimage = M * point\n\n# Extract the x and y coordinates of the image\nX, Y = image[0], image[1]\n\n# Simplify the expressions\nX_simplified = sp.simplify(X)\nY_simplified = sp.simplify(Y)\n\n# Express Y in terms of X\n# We know X = 2x - 1, so we solve for x in terms of X\nx_in_terms_of_X = sp.solve(X_simplified - (2*x - 1), x)[0]\nY_in_terms_of_X = Y_simplified.subs(x, x_in_terms_of_X)\n\n# Simplify the final expression\nY_in_terms_of_X_simplified = sp.simplify(Y_in_terms_of_X)\nprint(Y_in_terms_of_X_simplified)\n```\n```output\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\n\nReach max function call limit.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) that transforms the given vectors. Let's denote the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) as:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe know that:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n2a - b = 9 \\\\\n2c - d = 3\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\na - 3b = 7 \\\\\nc - 3d = -1\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe can solve these systems of equations to find \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\).\n\nFirst, let's solve the system for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n2a - b = 9 \\\\\na - 3b = 7\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this system using substitution or elimination. Let's use elimination. Multiply the first equation by 3 and subtract the second equation:\n\n\\[\n3(2a - b) - (a - 3b) = 3(9) - 7 \\implies 6a - 3b - a + 3b = 27 