es \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} \\]\n\nSubstituting the base and height into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 3 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 = 15 \\]\n\nSo, the area of the shaded triangle is \\(15 \\text{ cm}^2\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the base and height of the triangle\nbase = 10\nheight = 3\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * base * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n15.0\n```\nThe area of the shaded triangle is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the shaded triangle, we need to identify its base and height. From the diagram, we can see that the triangle is a right triangle with a base of 10 cm and a height of 3 cm. The area \\(A\\) of a triangle is given by the formula:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} \\]\nHere, the base is 10 cm and the height is 3 cm. So we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\\[ A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 3 \\]\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the base and height of the triangle\nbase = 10\nheight = 3\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * base * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n15.0\n```\nThe area of the shaded triangle is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the shaded triangle, we can use the formula for the area of a triangle, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n\\]\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that the base of the triangle is 10 cm and the height is 3 cm. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 3 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 = 15 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the base and height of the triangle\nbase = 10\nheight = 3\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * base * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```outp