s_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.0\n```\nThe class average on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.0}\\).", "To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n\\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{11}{4}\\) hours. So, we need to compute:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\nprint(distance)\n```\n```output\n137.5\n```\nThe distance traveled is 137.5 miles. To express this as a mixed number, we recognize that 137.5 is equivalent to \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]", 'To determine how far a car travels at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance traveled:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can calculate the distance by multiplying the speed by the time:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to its simplest form. We can do this by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) into a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[0]\ndenominator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[1]\n\n# Simplify the fraction\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, denominator)\nnumerator //= common_divisor\ndenominator //= common_divisor\n\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/{denominator}" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to its simplest form. We can divide both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the fractional part is in halves\n\n# Output the distance as a mixed number\ndistance_mixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/2"\nprint(distance_mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a time of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction. The mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) is equivalent to \\(\\frac{11}{4}\\) hours. Now we can substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4}\n\\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we can multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4}\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe fraction \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) is an improper fraction, so we convert it to a mixed number. To do this, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[\n275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ with a remainder of } 1\n\\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nThus, the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. The final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/2"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```', 'To determine how far a car travels at 50 miles per hour in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour and the time is \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction. The improper fraction equivalent of \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) is:\n\n\\[ 2\\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to a mixed number. We do this by dividing 550 by 4 to get the whole number part and the remainder will give us the fractional part.\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{550}{4} = 137\\frac{2}{4}\\). We can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nnumerator //= common_divisor\ndenominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Output the result\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number}{numerator}/{denominator}" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n1371/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction. \n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can calculate the distance by multiplying the speed (50 miles per hour) by the time (\\(\\frac{11}{4}\\) hours):\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) into a mixed number. To do this, we divide 550 by 4 to get the whole number part and the remainder will give us the fractional part.\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is \\(137 \\frac{2}{4}\\). We can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_denominator != 1 else f"{whole_number} {simplified_numerator}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', "To solve the problem of finding out how far a car travels at 50 miles per hour for $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ to an improper fraction.\n2. Multiply the speed (50 miles per hour) by the time ($2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours) to get the distance.\n3. Express the final answer as a mixed number.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nFirst, we convert $2\\frac{3}{4}$ to an improper fraction. The improper fraction form of $2\\frac{3}{4}$ is $\\frac{11}{4}$. \n\nNext, we multiply 50 by $\\frac{11}{4}$ to get the distance traveled.\n\nLet's do this calculation in Python.\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\n\n# Speed in miles per hour\nspeed = 50\n\n# Time in hours as a mixed number\ntime_mixed = Fraction(11, 4)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time_mixed\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\ndistance_mixed = (distance.numerator // distance.denominator, distance.numerator % distance.denominator, distance.denominator)\n\nprint((distance, distance_mixed))\n```\n```output\n(Fraction(275, 2), (137, 1, 2))\n```\nThe distance traveled by the car is $\\frac{275}{2}$ miles, which is equivalent to the mixed number $137\\frac{1}{2}$ miles.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]", 'To determine how far a car travels in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ to an improper fraction. The mixed number $2\\frac{3}{4}$ is equivalent to $\\frac{11}{4}$ hours.\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we multiply the numerator by 50 and keep the denominator the same:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction $\\frac{550}{4}$ by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction $\\frac{275}{2}$ to a mixed number. To do this, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part, and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo the mixed number is $137\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTherefore, the car would travel $137\\frac{1}{2}$ miles in $2\\frac{3}{4}$ hours.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', 'To determine how far a car travels at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour over a period of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance traveled:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction. The improper fraction equivalent of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) is:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can substitute the speed and time into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) into a mixed number. Since \\(275 \\div 2 = 137\\) with a remainder of 1, the mixed number is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code 