ance\n\nprint(min_distance)\n```\n```output\nKeyError: (\'D\', \'A\')\n```\nIt looks like there\'s an issue with the way the distances are being accessed. The KeyError indicates that the tuple (\'D\', \'A\') is not in the distances dictionary. This is because the dictionary only contains the distances for the edges that are explicitly defined. To fix this, we need to ensure that we handle all possible edges correctly.\n\nLet\'s update the code to handle all possible edges and ensure that we correctly calculate the total distance for each route.\n```python\n# Define the distances between the points\ndistances = {\n    (\'A\', \'B\'): 6, (\'A\', \'C\'): 6, (\'A\', \'D\'): 5,\n    (\'B\', \'C\'): 5, (\'B\', \'D\'): 3,\n    (\'C\', \'D\'): 4\n}\n\n# Function to calculate the total distance of a route\ndef calculate_distance(route):\n    total_distance = 0\n    for i in range(len(route) - 1):\n        if (route[i], route[i + 1]) in distances:\n            total_distance += distances[(route[i], route[i + 1])]\n        elif (route[i + 1], route[i]) in distances:\n            total_distance += distances[(route[i + 1], route[i])]\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f"Distance between {route[i]} and {route[i + 1]} is not defined.")\n    return total_distance\n\n# List of all possible routes starting from each point\nroutes = [\n    [\'A\', \'B\', \'C\', \'D\'], [\'A\', \'B\', \'D\', \'C\'], [\'A\', \'C\', \'B\', \'D\'], [\'A\', \'C\', \'D\', \'B\'], [\'A\', \'D\', \'B\', \'C\'], [\'A\', \'D\', \'C\', \'B\'],\n    [\'B\', \'A\', \'C\', \'D\'], [\'B\', \'A\', \'D\', \'C\'], [\'B\', \'C\', \'A\', \'D\'], [\'B\', \'C\', \'D\', \'A\'], [\'B\', \'D\', \'A\', \'C\'], [\'B\', \'D\', \'C\', \'A\'],\n    [\'C\', \'A\', \'B\', \'D\'], [\'C\', \'A\', \'D\', \'B\'], [\'C\', \'B\', \'A\', \'D\'], [\'C\', \'B\', \'D\', \'A\'], [\'C\', \'D\', \'A\', \'B\'], [\'C\', \'D\', \'B\', \'A\'],\n    [\'D\', \'A\', \'B\', \'C\'], [\'D\', \'A\', \'C\', \'B\'], [\'D\', \'B\', \'A\', \'C\'], [\