e cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the cube that has the shortest possible side lengths from which a steel sphere with a 3-inch radius can be made by removing metal from the corners of the cube.\n\nSince the sphere is inscribed within the cube, the diameter of the sphere will be equal to the side length of the cube. The diameter of the sphere is twice the radius, so the side length of the cube is \\(2 \\times 3 = 6\\) inches.\n\nThe volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by the formula \\(V = s^3\\). In this case, the side length \\(s\\) is 6 inches.\n\nLet's calculate the volume of the cube using Python.\n```python\n# Side length of the cube\nside_length = 6\n\n# Volume of the cube\nvolume_cube = side_length ** 3\nprint(volume_cube)\n```\n```output\n216\n```\nThe volume of the cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.", 'The volume of a sphere is given by the formula \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\), where \\(r\\) is the radius of the sphere. In this case, the radius of the sphere is 3 inches, so the volume of the sphere is \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (3)^3 = 36\\pi\\) cubic inches.\n\nThe cube that has the shortest possible side lengths and can contain the sphere must have a side length of 6 inches, since the diameter of the sphere is 6 inches. The volume of a cube is given by the formula \\(s^3\\), where \\(s\\) is the side length of the cube. Therefore, the volume of the cube is \\(6^3 = 216\\) cubic inches.\n\nTherefore, the volume of the cube is \\(\\boxed{216}\\) cubic inches.', "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of the cube that has the shortest possible side lengths from which a steel sphere with a 3-inch radius can be formed by removing metal from the corners of the cube. The sphere's diameter is twice the radius, so it is 6 inches. This means the side length of the cube must be at least 6 inches, because the sphere must fit entirely within the cube.\n\