l \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nx, p = sp.symbols('x p')\n\n# Define the function f(x)\nf = sp.Abs(x - p) + sp.Abs(x - 15) + sp.Abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\ninterval = (x, p, 15)\n\n# Evaluate f(x) at the boundaries\nf_at_p = f.subs(x, p)\nf_at_15 = f.subs(x, 15)\n\n# Simplify the function within the interval p <= x <= 15\nf_within_interval = sp.simplify(f.subs(x, 15))\n\n# The minimum value of f(x) in the interval p <= x <= 15\nmin_value = sp.Min(f_at_p, f_at_15, f_within_interval)\n\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\nMin(15, 30 - p)\n```\nThe output from the code indicates that the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is either 15 or \\( 30 - p \\). Since \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), the value \\( 30 - p \\) is always greater than 15. Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within the given interval. The function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of absolute value functions, and the critical points where the function might change its behavior are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to focus on the points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the function \\( f(x) \\) into different cases based on the value of \\( x \\):\n\n1. For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n\nSo, the function becomes:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the minimum value of \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\). Since \\( f(x) \\) is a decreasing function in this interval, the minimum value will occur at the right endpoint of the interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 5  # Example value for p, any value in the range 0 < p < 15 will work\nx_values = [p, 15]  # We only need to check the endpoints of the interval\n\n# Calculate the function values at the endpoints\nf_p = f(p, p)\nf_15 = f(15, p)\n\n# The minimum value of the function in the interval p <= x <= 15\nmin_value = min(f_p, f_15)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), where \\( 0 < p < 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. **Understand the Function:**\n   The function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) is composed of absolute value functions. The critical points where the behavior of the function changes are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\).\n\n2. **Analyze the Interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):**\n   Since \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we can simplify the absolute value expressions:\n   - For \\( x \\geq p \\), \\( |x - p| = x - p \\).\n   - For \\( x \\leq 15 \\), \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\).\n   - For \\( x \\leq p + 15 \\), \\( |x - p - 15| = p + 15 - x \\) (since \\( x \\leq 15 \\leq p + 15 \\)).\n\n   Therefore, for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the function simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (p + 15 - x) = 30 - x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the Minimum Value:**\n   The function \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing linear function. The minimum value in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) will occur at the right endpoint \\( x = 15 \\):\n   \\[\n   f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15\n   \\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\nx, p = sp.symbols('x p')\n\n# Define the function f(x)\nf = sp.Abs(x - p) + sp.Abs(x - 15) + sp.Abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\ninterval = (x, p, 15)\n\n# Simplify the function for the given interval\nf_simplified = sp.simplify(f.subs({sp.Abs(x - p): x - p, sp.Abs(x - 15): 15 - x, sp.Abs(x - p - 15): p + 15 - x}))\n\n# Find the minimum value in the interval\nmin_value = f_simplified.subs(x, 15)\n\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - (p + 15)| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval. The function involves three absolute value terms, and the critical points where the expressions inside the absolute values change sign are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we can simplify our analysis.\n\n1. For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\) because \\( x \\geq p \\).\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\) because \\( x \\leq 15 \\).\n   - \\( |x - (p + 15)| = (p + 15) - x \\) because \\( x \\leq p + 15 \\) (which is always true in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) since \\( p + 15 > 15 \\)).\n\nSo, the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + ((p + 15) - x) = x - p + 15 - x + p + 15 - x = 30 - x. \\]\n\nTo find the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at the endpoints of the interval:\n- At \\( x = p \\), \\( f(p) = 30 - p \\).\n- At \\( x = 15 \\), \\( f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\).\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function, the minimum value in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) occurs at \\( x = 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - (p + 15))\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 5  # Example value for p (0 < p < 15)\nx_values = [p, 15]  # Endpoints of the interval\n\n# Calculate the function values at the endpoints\nf_p = f(p, p)\nf_15 = f(15, p)\n\n# Determine the minimum value\nmin_value = min(f_p, f_15)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value taken by \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - (p + 15)| \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\). Let's break down the function based on the intervals defined by the points \\( p \\), \\( 15 \\), and \\( p + 15 \\).\n\n1. When \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = p + 15 - x \\)\n\nSo, the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (p + 15 - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nSince \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) will occur at the maximum value of \\( x \\) in this interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's calculate \\( f(15) \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\