ing linear function. Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) will occur at the right endpoint of the interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\).\n\n3. Substituting \\( x = 15 \\) into the function, we get:\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15. \\]\n\nSo the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 7  # Example value for p (0 < p < 15)\nx_values = range(p, 16)  # All integer values from p to 15\n\n# Calculate the minimum value of f(x) in the interval\nmin_value = min(f(x, p) for x in x_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval. The function involves absolute values, and the critical points where the behavior of the function changes are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since \\( x \\) is restricted to the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to consider the points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the function into different cases based on the value of \\( x \\):\n\n1. For \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\) (since \\( x \\leq 15 \\) and \\( p < 15 \\), \\( x - p - 15 \\) is negative)\n\nSo, the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function, its minimum value on the interval \\( p \\leq x \\l